  "worked_solution": "We have two pairs of vertical angles, and we know that vertical angles are congruent and therefore have the same measure. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠1 & =m∠2, \\\\ m∠3 & =m∠4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe are told that $m∠1={122}^{∘}$ and $m∠3={67}^{∘},$ so we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{122}^{∘} & =m∠2, \\\\ {67}^{∘} & =m∠4.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
